module nupp.suspension

--[[
Waiting without blocking the thread.

A suspension-aware call parks the frame it is in rather than stopping the
process, and whoever installed a handler decides what runs meanwhile -- an
event loop, a poll, the next frame.

```nupp:fragment
local suspension = require("nupp.suspension")

local function readLine(reader: Reader): string
    return suspension.suspend("example.readLine", function(
        resume: function(string),
        context: suspension.Context
    ): function()
        const subscription = reader:onLine(resume)

        return function(): nil
            subscription:release()
        end
    end)
end
```

`suspend` parks on something that will be ready later, `source` registers the
pump that makes it ready, `poll` drives every registered pump once, and
`handled` says whether a handler is listening;
without one, a park drives the registered pumps on this thread and blocks after
all. `canSuspend` answers whether a park would be permitted here at all, and
`create` makes a coroutine that inherits the handler.

Installing a handler, and driving the parks it accepts, is the other side of
this: [](nupp.suspension.host). A library needs none of it.

This is the layer underneath. Somewhere to put children discovered over time,
with one answer for failure and cancellation, is [](nupp.tasks); real
parallelism is [](nupp.workers). Come here directly to make a library waitable,
or to write a combinator neither of those has.

An arbitrary blocking Lua or C call still blocks the thread. A library opts in
by parking through this module; nothing intercepts calls that do not.

See [suspension.md](docs/learn/runtime/concurrency/suspension.md).
]]

local contract = require("nupp.suspension.spi")
local selected = require("nupp.suspension.selected")

local provider = selected.provider
local suspension = {}

--- A readiness pump, and the handle that owns its lifetime.
type suspension.Source = contract.Source

--- What a library is handed while it subscribes.
type suspension.Context = contract.Context

suspension.Source = contract.Source
suspension.Context = contract.Context

--- Registers a readiness pump outside any subscription.
suspension.source = provider.source

--- Drives every registered pump once, and answers how many things settled.
---
--- Beside `source` because they are the two halves of one registry: a scheduler
--- drains what libraries registered, and so does an embedding host driving a
--- component that only ever waits.
suspension.poll = provider.poll

--- Subscribes once, then waits for one typed result through the active handler.
suspension.suspend = provider.suspend

--- Whether a handler is installed here, which is what `blocking` against
--- `cooperative` means to a caller deciding before it commits to waiting.
suspension.handled = provider.handled

--- Whether a suspension performed here would be permitted, handler barriers included.
suspension.canSuspend = provider.canSuspend

--- Creates a coroutine that inherits the handler installed where it was created.
---
--- Here as well as on [](nupp.suspension.host) because the compiler emits it: a
--- `with` statement's cleanup runs in a coroutine, and generated code names this
--- module to make it. Scheduler authors want it beside the rest of the host surface;
--- the emitted call wants it where it has always been.
suspension.create = provider.create

export = suspension
